{"id":"0e49ef470c93837f","group":"58","path":"58/batch04/58-cor-dedekind.md","title":"A Dedekind Cut Determines a Unique Dedekind Real","display":"cor-dedekind — A Dedekind Cut Determines a Unique Dedekind Real","type":"corollary","metadata":{"type":"corollary","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-cor-dedekind","aliases":["58-cor-dedekind"],"display":"cor-dedekind — A Dedekind Cut Determines a Unique Dedekind Real","depends_on":["[[../batch17/58-df-dedekind-cut.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"corollary"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-cor-dedekind"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-cor-dedekind</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"cor-dedekind — A Dedekind Cut Determines a Unique Dedekind Real"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"37d8cf418a7b6598\" href=\"?note=37d8cf418a7b6598\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-dedekind-cut.md\">../batch17/58-df-dedekind-cut.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A,B\\subseteq\\mathbb Q\">\\(A,B\\subseteq\\mathbb Q\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x\\in V\">\\(x\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DedekindCut}_S(A,B)\">\\(\\mathrm{DedekindCut}_S(A,B)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R_D=\\operatorname{DedekindCuts}(\\mathbb Q)\">\\(\\mathbb R_D=\\operatorname{DedekindCuts}(\\mathbb Q)\\)</span> are from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"37d8cf418a7b6598\" href=\"?note=37d8cf418a7b6598\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-dedekind-cut.md\">../batch17/58-df-dedekind-cut.md</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DedekindRealOf}_S\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{DedekindRealOf}_S\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> is the graph predicate defined here.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}dedekind\\text{-}graph}\\vdash \\mathrm{DedekindRealOf}_S(x,A,B)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{DedekindCut}_S(A,B)\\land x\\in\\mathbb R_D\\land x=A\\land B=\\mathbb Q\\setminus A.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}dedekind\\text{-}graph}\\vdash \\mathrm{DedekindRealOf}_S(x,A,B)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{DedekindCut}_S(A,B)\\land x\\in\\mathbb R_D\\land x=A\\land B=\\mathbb Q\\setminus A.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}dedekind}\\vdash\\forall A,B\\subseteq\\mathbb Q\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{DedekindCut}_S(A,B)\\to\\exists!x\\in\\mathbb R_D\\;\\mathrm{DedekindRealOf}_S(x,A,B)\\bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}dedekind}\\vdash\\forall A,B\\subseteq\\mathbb Q\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{DedekindCut}_S(A,B)\\to\\exists!x\\in\\mathbb R_D\\;\\mathrm{DedekindRealOf}_S(x,A,B)\\bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>In the Dedekind construction the real determined by the cut is literally its lower part <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span>; the upper part is <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb Q\\setminus A\">\\(\\mathbb Q\\setminus A\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Order-completeness statements require an explicit rational-to-real embedding and the inclusion order on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R_D\">\\(\\mathbb R_D\\)</span>; no untyped rational/cut comparison is used here.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch17/58-df-dedekind-cut.md","status":"resolved","id":"37d8cf418a7b6598","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-dedekind-cut.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-dedekind-cut.md","status":"resolved","id":"37d8cf418a7b6598","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{DedekindCut}_S(A,B)$ and $\\mathbb R_D=\\operatorname{DedekindCuts}(\\mathbb Q)$ are from [[../batch17/58-df-dedekind-cut.md]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"A,B\\subseteq\\mathbb Q","display":false},{"tex":"x\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{DedekindCut}_S(A,B)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R_D=\\operatorname{DedekindCuts}(\\mathbb Q)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{DedekindRealOf}_S\\subseteq V^3","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}dedekind\\text{-}graph}\\vdash \\mathrm{DedekindRealOf}_S(x,A,B)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{DedekindCut}_S(A,B)\\land x\\in\\mathbb R_D\\land x=A\\land B=\\mathbb Q\\setminus A.","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}dedekind}\\vdash\\forall A,B\\subseteq\\mathbb Q\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{DedekindCut}_S(A,B)\\to\\exists!x\\in\\mathbb R_D\\;\\mathrm{DedekindRealOf}_S(x,A,B)\\bigr).","display":true},{"tex":"A","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb Q\\setminus A","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R_D","display":false}],"bytes":1285,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-46","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch04/58-cor-dedekind.md|58-cor-dedekind]]（batch04）"}],"outgoing":["37d8cf418a7b6598"]}